# One person, four git identities — collapsed for git's reading tools.
#
# Machines got configured at different times and drifted: this repo alone
# carries commits under `murty`, `Murty`, `Shalafi` and a work identity, and
# `git shortlog -sne` counts them as four contributors. Worse, the trick used
# elsewhere to tell my commits from a colleague's is `git log --format=%an` —
# see factory-backend — and that check is only as good as the name being one
# name.
#
# This changes no commit. It is read at display time by log, shortlog, blame
# and friends; the commit objects keep whatever they were authored with, and
# GitHub's own UI does not read this file at all.
#
# Mapping is by **email**, which is the stable half — so no name needs to be
# written here, and the first line normalises `murty` vs `Murty` on its own.
#
# install.sh also points `mailmap.file` at this file globally, so the same
# mapping applies in every repo on the machine without committing anything
# into them.

murty <murty206@gmail.com> <murty206@gmail.com>
murty <murty206@gmail.com> <muharrem.arli@nurolmakina.com.tr>
